{"products":[{"id":"7c7fa1ea-0730-4e0c-829b-2d50a1f3c776","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["0E5A5DFF-7518-494A-AD5E-7C20A1F98FFD","242191AB-2749-4585-A09B-C274A1C196D8","288624C3-E0C0-4816-86A1-57B068E20D5F"],"areaId":"5bccb549615b033152a53370b17e399fac993639dd32c49b9376e2079da84104","issueDateTime":"2026-11-09T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-10T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-10T23:30:00Z","content":"<p>Avalanche conditions are generally safe. Avoid isolated pockets of wind-drifted snow above treeline. You may encounter wet, loose avalanches on steep south and southwest aspects in the afternoon, particularly near rock outcrops.</p><p></p>"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"428bf121-91ef-5607-86a2-c57b18bbb0af","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1793825477/AvIDfx/apwek65cnbiqmdfdombu.webp","width":1612,"height":1209,"credit":"","caption":"<p>Our most recent reported human-triggered avalanche occurred outside of Silverton on Tuesday, November 3rd right after the storm. This soft slab avalanche in Velocity Basin was triggered by a snowboarder who was caught, carried, and partially buried. It serves as an early-season warning that, even though its barely November, there is now enough snow in our mountains to be concerned about avalanches that could be large enough to bury, injure, or kill a human.</p>","tag":"avalanche","altText":"An avalanche in a alpine bowl with a person in the debris towards the bottom. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-03T20:51:18.057Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"1cfc1017-c1fd-5e25-9ea3-039aba70f8ed","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1793740560/AvIDfx/v1wbgixz6ted2iljevzo.webp","width":514,"height":685,"credit":"Chris Dickson","caption":"<p>This Storm Slab avalanche occurred during the last snowfall event on Sunday, November 2nd in the Ophir area. These types of slabs have been eroded away by the faceting process under continued mild weather. </p>","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A rugged, snow-covered mountainside with exposed rocky ridges. Deep blue shadows contrast with brightly sunlit snow across the steep slopes, and a path of disturbed snow from a recent avalanche or slide is visible in the lower basin.","dateTaken":"2026-11-03T21:21:09.352Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"1f787fc4-9a32-5dd3-a8b5-2fe48d43cbb5","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1793998137/AvIDfx/jwoeie8wmabortgognfe.webp","width":2500,"height":3333,"credit":"","caption":"<p>Our last storm brought a lot of rain and then eventually some snowfall to our mountains. Large wet loose avalanches were reported after the skies cleared, including this one on Red Mountain 3 in the northern San Juan Mountains. As temperatures drop and the snowpack refreezes, wet loose activity is no longer on the menu. </p>","tag":"avalanche","altText":"An avalanche debris piled covered in fresher snowfall on a sunlit mountain. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-05T20:51:36Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"b13fcacb-914d-582e-948a-0cf42e452320","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794173247/AvIDfx/f3cexyq8djmcrcdnjcwl.webp","width":350,"height":263,"credit":"","caption":"<p>This recently reported avalanche from The Battleship slide path near Silverton was estimated to have occurred within the last five days. This is a northwest facing near treeline slope.</p>","tag":"avalanche","altText":"avalanche","dateTaken":"2026-11-07T21:28:18.613Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-10T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-11T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}}],"areas":{"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"5bccb549615b033152a53370b17e399fac993639dd32c49b9376e2079da84104","type":"Feature","bbox":[-108.4359443866,36.9925681097,-106.1568922216,38.388209885],"geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-108.4359443866,37.7564463878],[-108.4343396793,